  nonce: f5d7  # f5d7
  message: "Strict-mode drift linter shipped in PR (commit aa5ed053d). axis_drift.find_drift gains optional axis-principle enforcement via allowed_axis_names + name_to_axis params; edge_types.find_axis_drift gains a strict=True kw enabling {relationship, pending_classification} as the allowed set (permissive pending per the design). scripts/check-edge-type-drift gains --strict. Implementation field-agnostic — future Symbol.kind / evidence_type axes inherit the pattern via the axis_drift kwargs. 3 known-pending off-axis consumer references pinned by test_find_axis_drift_strict_known_off_axis_consumers (http_calls in compact, grpc_calls in taint + io_boundary; load-bearing because http.py/grpc.py producers still emit those endpoint_shape values pending future Phase-3-style migrations). The .githooks/pre-commit flip from default-lax to --strict is governance work pending separate human approval (filed as needs_human_review per AGENTS.md governance rules)."  # f5d7
